From d7434605f9c14cd8c74041b8ee62bfcb26977ad8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:07:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: verisilicon: Copy the buffer metadata before a job can
 fail

device_run() copies the timestamp, flags and timecode of the OUTPUT
buffer to the CAPTURE buffer only after it has acquired a core, resumed
it and enabled its clocks. When any of these steps fails, the job is
finished with both buffers in the error state, and the CAPTURE buffer
is returned with the timestamp of whatever frame it held before.

Userspace pairs a CAPTURE buffer with its frame by the timestamp, also
when the buffer carries V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR: GStreamer's v4l2 decoders
and encoders drop the frame named by the timestamp of a failed buffer.
A stale timestamp makes them drop the wrong frame, or none, and leaves
the failed frame pending.

Copy the metadata first, so every buffer the job returns carries the
timestamp of its frame.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
index 2d7ea42d2629..27e218bc3e9a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
@@ -264,6 +264,12 @@ static void device_run(void *priv)
 	src = hantro_get_src_buf(ctx);
 	dst = hantro_get_dst_buf(ctx);
 
+	/*
+	 * Copy the timestamp before anything can fail: userspace matches a
+	 * CAPTURE buffer returned with an error to its frame by it.
+	 */
+	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst);
+
 	core = hantro_acquire_core(ctx);
 	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!core))
 		goto err_cancel_job;
@@ -279,8 +285,6 @@ static void device_run(void *priv)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_pm_put;
 
-	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst);
-
 	if (ctx->codec_ops->run(ctx))
 		goto err_clk_disable;
 
-- 
2.55.0

